<title>INDONESIA: Indonesia considers tax breaks for auto parts.</title>
<headline>Indonesia considers tax breaks for auto parts.</headline>
<dateline>JAKARTA 1996-09-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indonesia is considering offering tax incentives for automobile spare-parts vendors, Bisnis Indonesia newspaper reported on Monday.</p>
<p>The newspaper quoted Investment Minister Sanyoto Sastrowardoyo as saying the vendors should meet certain requirements set by a tax committee to be eligible for the breaks.</p>
<p>&quot;If the vendors meet the requirements and submit the proposal to get the tax holiday, the proposals will certainly be considered,&quot; Sastrowardoyo was quoted as saying.</p>
<p>Sanyoto declined to give details of the move saying it was still being discussed.</p>
<p>--- Jakarta newsroom +6221 384-6364</p>
